hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5116","Amr bin Mansour and Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, On the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ma`bad al-Qasas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Jadali, who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: “If he drinks alcohol, flog him, then if he does it again, flog him, then if he does it again, flog him, then if he does it a fourth time.” So kill him.” And the wording is from Amr. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5117","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn 'Umar, and a group of the Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks again, flog him; then if he drinks again, flog him; then if he drinks again, kill him."""
"5118","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Raqqashi told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq. On the authority of Abdullah bin Utba bin Urwa bin Masoud Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, flog him, then if he drinks, kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5119","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “If a man drinks, flog him, and if he returns So flog him, and if he returns the fourth time, kill him. Then a man from among us was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, but he did not kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5120","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Hurashi told us, he said: Ziyad told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir, he said: he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever drinks alcohol, beat him, and if he repeats it, beat him. So they beheaded him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, struck Na’im four times, and the Muslims saw that the punishment had taken place, and that murder had occurred. \has been lifted up\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5121","Abu Dawud Suleiman bin Saif Al-Harrani told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, he said: We attended with Ibn Abbas the funeral of Maimuna, the husband of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with great honor. Ibn Abbas said: “This is Maimuna, if you raise her funeral, so do not disturb it, and do not disturb it, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: had nine women with him, and he used to swear for eight, and one to which he did not divide.\ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5122","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari told us, on the authority of Yazid, who was the son of Zurayi. He said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, that Anas He told them that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to go around his wives in one night, and he had nine wives on that day.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5123","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I was jealous of the women who gave themselves to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I would say: Will the free woman give herself up?” So God revealed God Almighty: You may hope for whomever you wish of them and give shelter to yourself whomever you wish. I said: By God, I do not see your Lord but hastening for you in your desires. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5124","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub Al-Jawzjani told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Sufyan, who is Ibn Uyaynah, told us, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died and he had nine wives.” It will happen to them, except for Sawda, for she gave her day and night to Aisha.”"
"5125","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abu Hazim told us, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, he said: I am in The people, when a woman said, “I have given myself to you, O Messenger of God, so decide what you think about it.” Then a man stood up and said: Marry her to me. He said: Go and ask for even an iron ring. He went and did not find anything, not even an iron ring. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I will take you. Is there any surah of the Qur’an? He said: Yes. He said: So he married it to whatever surahs of the Qur’an he had with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5126","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid and Musa bin Ali told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, He said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told me that Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered He, peace and blessings be upon him, decided to choose his wives. He started with me and said: I have mentioned a matter to you, so do not be in a hurry until you ask your parents for advice. She said: He knew that my parents would not order me to separate from him. She said: Then he recited this verse: “O Prophet, tell your wives, if they are You want the life of this world and its adornments, so come, I will give you pleasure and give you a pleasant release. So I said: What of this should I consult my parents about? For I want God and His Messenger and the Hereafter. Aisha said: Then the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did the same as I did, but it was not That is when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said it to them, and they chose to divorce him for the reason that they chose him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5127","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Musa bin Ayan told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri. He said: Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that she told him that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He came to her when God commanded him to tell his wives.” Aisha said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, started with me. He said: I am mentioning a matter to you, so do not be in a hurry until you ask your parents for advice. She said: He knew that my parents do not order me to separate from him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Prophet, tell your wives, if you desire the life of this world and its adornments, then come and I will give you pleasure. So I said: I ask my parents about this, for I want God and His Messenger and the Hereafter. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5128","Bishr ibn Khalid told us, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a choice to his wives and it was a divorce?”"
"5129","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Stolen, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us a choice, so we chose him, and there was no divorce.”"
"5130","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: We preserved it from Amr, on the authority of Ata’, he said: Aisha said: “The Messenger of God did not die May God bless him and grant him peace until women are made lawful to him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Ibn Jurayj entered between Ata’ and Aisha Ubaid bin Umair. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5131","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, and he is Al-Mughirah bin Salamah Al-Makhzoumi, he said: Wahib told us, he said: we told him: Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not die until God had made it lawful He has the right to marry as many women as he wants.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5132","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Ulayya, he said: Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubaid, told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, said: I was with Ibn Masoud while he was with Uthman, and Uthman said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Meaning: young men, so he said: Whoever of you is tall, let him get married, for it will sharpen the gaze and improve chastity, and whoever is not, then fasting. He had a come, “Suleiman bin Mihran disagreed with him.”"
"5133","Ahmad bin Harb Al-Mawsili told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, he said: I was walking with Abdullah was in Mina, and Othman met him, and he stood with him and spoke to him. He said: “O Abu Abdul Rahman, shall I not marry you to a young slave girl? Perhaps she will You remember some of the past, so Abdullah said: As for if you said that, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: O group of young men who If he is able to marry you, let him get married.”"
"5134","Harun bin Ishaq al-Kufi told me, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “Whoever of you is able to do so, let him marry, and whoever cannot He is able to do so by fasting, for it is a reward for him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: The black one in this hadith is not preserved. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5135","Bishr bin Khalid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, “that Othman said to Ibn Masoud: “Do you have a girl that I can marry to you? So Abdullah called Alqamah, and it was narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever is able to do so, let him get married, for he is more likely to “For sight, and for the protection of chastity, and whoever is not able, let him fast, for it is a reward for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5136","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “O young men, whoever among you is able to do so, let him get married, for he lower my gaze and protect my chastity, and whoever does not, let him fast, for fasting has a reward for him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5137","Muhammad bin Al-Ala told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: “O young men, whoever among you is able to do good, let him get married,” and he cited the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5138","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “forbade celibacy.” Ash’ath ibn Abd al-Malik disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5139","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, On the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade celibacy.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Qatada is more steadfast and more protected than anyone else. Ash'ath, and this Hadith of Ash'ath is more like the authentic one, and God knows best."
"5140","Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded to Othman, who was the son of the celibate Mazun, and if he had given him permission, we would have chosen him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5141","Yahya bin Musa told us, he said: Anas bin Iyadh told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Abu Hurairah, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, “I am a young man and I fear hardship for myself, and I cannot find the courage to marry women. Should I be circumcised?” Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, turned away from him, until he said three, then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Abu Hurairah, dry the pen with what you are worthy of. So limit yourself to that or leave it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Awza’i did not hear this hadith from Al-Zuhri, and this is an authentic hadith. Narrated by Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5142","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, “that A group of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Some of them said: I do not marry women. Some of them said: I do not eat meat. Some of them said: I do not sleep. On a bed, and some of them said: I will fast and will not break my fast. This was conveyed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he thanked God and praised him, then, He said: What is the matter with people who say such-and-such, but I pray and sleep, and I fast and break my fast, and I marry women, so whoever deviates from my Sunnah \It is not from me\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5143","Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Khalanji told us, he said: Abu Sa’id, the client of Banu Hashim, told us: Husayn bin Nafi’ Al-Mazni told us, he said Al-Hasan Al-Basri narrated to me, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, that he entered upon the Mother of the Believers, Aisha. I said: “I want to ask you about Celibacy, what do you think of it? She said: So do not do it, have you not heard God Almighty say: And We sent messengers before you and appointed for them. Spouses and offspring, so do you not become celibate? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5144","Qutaibah bin Sa’id Abu Raja’ al-Baghlani told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, meaning Ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There are three rights that God Almighty has incumbent upon them: their assistance: the office of one who wants to deliver, And the married man who desires chastity, and the one who strives in the cause of God.”"
"5145","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad, he is Ibn Zaid, told us, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “I got married, So I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Did you get married, Jabir? I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a married man? I said: No, but a married man? He said: “Then you are welcome, a virgin, that you may play with her and she may play with you.”"
"5146","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Habib, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, met me. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “O Jabir, have you married a woman after me?” I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: Early or later? I said: Either. He said: “Would you like a virgin to play with you?”"
"5147","Al-Hussein bin Harith Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, On the authority of his father, he said: “Abu Bakr and Omar, may God be pleased with them, proposed to Fatima, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: She is young. Then Ali proposed to her and married her to him.”"
"5148","Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam al-Tarsusi told us, he said: Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith told us, he said: I heard my father, he said: Hussein told us. The teacher, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, he said: Aamir bin Sharahil Al-Shabi told me, that he heard Fatima bint Qais, and she was one of the The first female emigrants said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf proposed to me among a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God proposed to me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon his master, Usama bin Zaid. I was told that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever loves me, Let him love Osama. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to me, I said: My command is in your hand, so marry me to whomever you wish.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5149","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: I am Al-Hakam bin Nafi’, he said: Shuaib, meaning Ibn Abi Hamza, told me on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr told me, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah ibn Rabi’ah ibn Abd Shams, and he was among those who witnessed Badr With the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he adopted Salim and married him to his brother’s daughter, Hind bint al-Walid bin Rabi’ah. A slave of a woman from the Ansar, just as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zaid, and whoever adopted a man in pre-Islamic times, people called him To him, and bequeathed his inheritance until God revealed about that: Call them by their fathers. This is more equitable in the sight of God. If you do not know their fathers, then your brothers. In religion, and your friends, return them to their fathers. He who has no known father is a friend and a brother in religion.”"
"5150","Kathir ibn Ubaid al-Humsi told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb told us, on the authority of al-Zubaidi, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba “that Abdullah bin Amr bin Uthman divorced when he was a young boy in the emirate of Marwan, the daughter of Sa’id bin Zayd, and her mother was Bint Qays.” Of course, so her aunt Fatima bint Qais sent her ordering her to move from the house of Abdullah bin Amr, and Marwan heard about that. So he sent for Sa`id's daughter, who ordered her to return to her place, and asked her what prompted her to move before she observed the waiting period. Her residence until her waiting period is over. So she sent to him informing him that her maternal aunt Fatima bint Qais had given her a fatwa to that effect, and he sent Marwan. Qubaysah bin Dhu’ayb went to Fatima to ask her about this. Fatima bint Qays claimed that she was under the supervision of Abu Amr bin Hafs, so when The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered Ali bin Abi Talib to go to Yemen with him and send her a divorce, which is the remainder of her divorce, and he ordered Al-Harith ibn Hisham and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi’ah were responsible for her maintenance, so she sent a message to Al-Harith and Ayyash to ask them who had ordered it. Her husband, and they said: No, by God, she has no obligation to support us unless she is pregnant, and she does not have the right to be in our dwelling except with our permission. She claimed that she had come to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so she mentioned that to him, and he believed them. Fatima said: Where shall I move, O? Messenger of God? He said: Go with Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind man whom God Almighty has named in his book. Fatima said: So I stayed with him. He was a man whose sight had gone, and I used to leave my clothes with him until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her to Usama bin Zaid. Marwan denied that to her and said: I have not heard this hadith from anyone before you, and I will adhere to the infallibility that we found the people to believe. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5151","Imran bin Bakkar bin Rashid Al-Homsi told us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that Abu Hudhayfah ibn Utbah ibn Rabi’ah ibn Abd Sun, and he was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He adopted Salim, and married him to his brother’s daughter Hind bint al-Walid ibn Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams, who was the client of an Ansar woman, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zaid. And whoever adopted a man in pre-Islamic times, people would invite him to their place, and inherit from his inheritance, until God Almighty revealed about that: Call them to their fathers. He is fairer in the sight of God. If you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your followers. So whoever has no known father is a friend and a brother in religion. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5152","Muhammad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ayoub bin Sulaiman bin Bilal told us, he said: Abu Bakr bin Abi Uwais told me, on the authority of Sulayman, he Ibn Bilal, he said: Yahya said, and Ibn Shihab told me, he said: Urwa bin al-Zubayr and Ibn Abdullah bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: that Abu Hudhayfah bin Utbah bin Rabi’ah bin Abd Shams, who was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted a safe family, and he was the slave of a woman from the Ansar, as “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, adopted Zaid bin Haritha, and Abu Hudhayfah bin Rabi’ah Salim married his brother Hind’s daughter. Al-Walid bin Utba bin Rabia, and Hind bint Al-Walid bin Rabia was one of the first emigrants, and she was one of my best days at that time. Quraysh, when God Almighty revealed regarding Zayd ibn Haritha, “Call them by their fathers. It is fairer in the sight of God.” He rejected every one of those who belonged to His father, and if his father is not known, he shall be returned to his master.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5153","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Abu Tamila, whose name is Yahya bin Wadh, told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the people of the world are the ones who give money to them.”"
"5154","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Jahdari told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, “that he married A woman at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, met him and said: “Have you gotten married, O Jabir?” He said: I said: Yes. He said: A virgin or a married man? I said: Rather, a virgin. He said: Would you like a virgin to play with you? He said: I said: O Messenger of God, have sisters for me, so I was afraid that you would come between me and them. He said: So then, a woman is married to Her religion, her wealth, and her beauty, so you must adhere to the same religion, may your hands be rubbed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5155","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa`id al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abi Sa`id, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A woman may be married to four people: for her money, for her according to her, And for her beauty and her religion, so adhere to the same religion, may your hands be blessed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5156","Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, who was a strong man, and he used to carry prisoners from Mecca to Medina, said: “So I called a man To carry him, and there was a prostitute in Mecca called Anak, and she was his friend. She approached and saw darkness in the shadow of the wall, so she said: Who is this? Marthad, welcome and welcome, Marthad. Go out tonight and spend the night with us in the camp. I said: O Anak, God has forbidden adultery. She said: O Anak. People of the tents, this pampered man, this one who carries your captives from Mecca to Medina. So I took the server, and he asked me for eight. So they came until they stood on my head, and they urinated, and their urine flew on me, and God blinded them to me, so I came to my friend and carried him, and when I finished I took him to Arak, so I untied him, then I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I said: O Messenger of God, shall I marry a hug? So he remained silent about me, so she revealed: “And no one can marry an adulteress except an adulterer or a polytheist.” So he called me and recited it to me, and said: “Do not marry her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5157","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Al-Nadr bin Shumayl, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: I am Harun bin Riab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of God, “There is a beautiful woman under me, who does not repel the hand of a toucher. He said: Divorce her. He said: I cannot be patient with her. He said: So keep her. Yazid bin Harun disagreed with him."
"5158","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Harun, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, And others, on the authority of Harun bin Riab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, and Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, Abdul Karim attributed it to Ibn Abbas, but Aaron did not attribute it to him. They said: A man came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “I have a woman who is one of the people dearest to me, and she does not withhold the hand of someone who touches her.” He said: “Divorce her.” He said: “I will not be patient with her.” He said: Enjoy it.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith is not proven, and Abd al-Karim is not strong, and Harun bin Riyab is proven. He sent the hadith from him, and Aaron is trustworthy and his hadith is more authentic than the hadith of Abd al-Karim. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5159","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, Al-Nadr informed us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abu Talha, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, they said: O Messenger of God, “Will you not marry one of the women of the Ansar?” He said: “Indeed, there is intense jealousy among them.”"
"5160","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Raqqi al-Qattan told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Al-Muslim bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Qurrah, on the authority of Maqil bin Yasar, said: A man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I I met a woman of rank and position, but she does not give birth. Should I marry her? He forbade it, then he brought him a second wife. He forbade it, then he brought it to him? The third time, he said: “Marry the kind and gentle ones, for I will be proud of you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5161","Qutaibah bin Sa’id told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: It was said to the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Which of the women is best?” He said: “The one who pleases him when he looks, who obeys him when he commands, and does not disagree with him regarding herself and her wealth.” \with what he hates\"""""
"5162","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Haywa, meaning Ibn Shurayh, told us, and he mentioned another, they said: Shurahbil bin Sharik informed us that he heard Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali speaking, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin al-Aas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, the whole world is enjoyment, and the best enjoyment in the world is a righteous woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5163","Abd al-Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaym al-Dimashqi, the judge of Ramla, informed us. He said: Marwan, who is the son of Muawiyah al-Fazari, informed us. He said: He told us. Yazid, meaning Ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: “A man proposed to a woman from the Ansar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: He, peace and blessings be upon him: Did you look at it? He said: No, so he ordered him to look at it. Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is Abu Hazim’s name. Salman is the client of Izza Kufi, and the name of Abu Hazim Al-Madini is Salama bin Dinar, and he is the father of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Hazim"
"5164","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah al-Marwazi informed us, Abu Rizmah’s name is Ghazwan, he said: Hafs ibn Ghayath told us, he said: Asim, meaning Ibn Sulaiman Al-Ahwal, narrated to us on the authority of Bakr Ibn Abdullah Al-Muzani, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah, who said: “I proposed to a woman... The era of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Have you looked at it? I said: No. He said: Then look at it, for it is more worthy. That there be harmony between you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5165","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid Al-Muqri informed us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that a man wanted to marry a woman, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Look at her, for in the eyes of the women of the Ansar \Something\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5166","Muhammad bin Adam told us, he said: Ali bin Hashim bin Al-Barid told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: A man from the Ansar came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: “I married a woman.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Didn’t you look at it, for there was something in the eyes of the Ansar” that Ali bin Hashim bin Al-Barid disagreed with. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5167","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told me, he said: Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, he said: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that a man said: O Messenger of God, “I married one of the Ansar.” He said: Didn’t you look at her? In the eyes of the Ansar there is nothing.”"
"5168","Hajib bin Sulaiman al-Munbiji told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, meaning the one-eyed son of Muhammad, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, And Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Abu Salamah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman bin Awf, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Thawban They asked Fatima bint Qais about her situation, and she said: “My husband divorced me three times, and the agent said: You have neither housing nor maintenance.” She said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: You have no place of residence or maintenance. You must observe the waiting period with Ibn Umm Maktum. Then... When I came, I called him to my ears. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Who has engaged to you? So I said: Muawiyah and another man From Quraysh, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for Muawiyah, he is a boy from Quraysh who has nothing, and as for the other: he is a companion of evil and no good. In it, but marry Usama bin Zaid. She said: I hated him. He said: That was three times, so I married him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5169","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, I read it while I was listening, and the pronunciation is by Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, On the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Fatima bint Qais, “that Abu Amr bin Hafs divorced her absolutely while he was absent, so he sent His agent came to her with barley, and she displeased him. He said: By God, you have nothing against us. So she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned. That is for him, so he said: You have no maintenance, so he ordered her to observe the waiting period in the house of a partner’s mother. Then, he said: This is a woman who is being cheated on by my friends, so observe the waiting period. With Ibn Umm Maktoum, for he is a blind man. You put on your clothes, so when you undress, then inform me. She said: When I undressed, I mentioned to him that Muawiyah Ibn Abi Sufyan and Abu Al-Jahm addressed me, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for Abu Jahm, he should not remove his staff from his shoulders. As for Muawiyah: He is a vagabond who has no money, but marry Usama bin Zaid, and I hated him. Then he said: Marry Usama bin Zaid, so I married him. So God made good in him, and she was happy with him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5170","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed Abu Qudamah told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Saeed Al-Thawri, he said: He told me Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwa, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me.” He greeted him in Shawwal, and I entered upon him in Shawwal, so which of his wives was more fortunate with him than me?"
"5171","Abdul-Rahman bin Muhammad bin Salam told me, he said: Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told me, he said: I heard my father, he said: Hussein told us. The teacher, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, he said: Aamir bin Sharahil Al-Shabi told me, that he heard Fatima bint Qais, and she was one of the The first female emigrants said: “Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf proposed to me among a group of the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God proposed to me. May God’s prayers and peace be upon his master, Usama bin Zaid. I was told that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever loves me, Let him love Osama. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spoke to me, I said: My command is in your hands, so marry me to whomever you wish. He said: Go to Umm A partner, and the mother of a partner was a rich woman from the Ansar, who spent a lot of money in the cause of God Almighty, and guests would come to her. So I said: I will do it. He said: Do not do that, for Umm Sharik has many guests, and I would hate for your veil to fall off or for the garment to be revealed on your legs. The people will see some of what you dislike about you, but go to your cousin Abdullah bin Amr bin Umm Maktoum, and he is a man from the tribe of Bani Umm Maktum. Fahr, so I moved to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5172","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “He does not engage “One of you is engaged to one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5173","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim said: Malik told me, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “None of you should propose to his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5174","Muhammad ibn Mansour al-Makki and Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not quarrel, nor should a present man sell to a distant one, nor should a man sell on the basis of his brother’s sale, nor He proposes his brother’s proposal, and the woman does not ask for a divorce from her sister so that what is in her vessel will be sufficient.” The wording is by Sa’id. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5175","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: he told me Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “None of you should propose to his brother until he gets married.” \or leave\"""""
"5176","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, meaning Ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “A man should not name someone else.” “He will marry his brother, and he will not propose to his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5177","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “None of you should propose to his brother.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5178","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Masisi told me, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, Ibn Juraij said: I heard Nafi’ narrated that Abdullah bin Omar, He used to say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the sale of some of you in exchange for the sale of others, and a man should not propose to another man until he abandons his marriage.” The suitor accepts him, or the suitor gives him permission.”"
"5179","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Marhum ibn Abdul Aziz al-Attar Abu Abdullah told me, saying: I heard Thabit al-Bunani, saying I was with Anas bin Malik, who has a daughter of his, and he said: “A woman came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and proposed to him.” She asked herself, “O Messenger of God, do you need me?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5180","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Marhum told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, “that a woman presented herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Peace be upon him. Anas’s daughter laughed and said: How modest she was. Anas said: She is better than you. She presented herself to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5181","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh informed us, he said: Abdul Razzaq informed us, he said: Muammar informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, said: “Hafsa, Omar’s daughter, became a slave of Khunnis, and he was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and was among those who witnessed Badr. He died in Medina, and I met Uthman bin Affan and proposed to him as Hafsa. I said: If you wish, I will make Hafsa your wife. He said: I will look into it. That is, so I stayed for Laila and met him, and he said: I do not want to get married on this day. Omar said: I met Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him. So I said: If you wish, I will make you marry Hafsa, but he did not return anything to me, so I was more generous to him than I was to Uthman, may God be pleased with him, so I remained nights, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to her, so I married her to him, and then Abu Bakr met me and said: Perhaps you found something against me. When you proposed to me Hafsa, but I did not return anything to you, I said: Yes, he said: He did not prevent me when you proposed to me from returning anything to you, except I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mention it, and I would not have revealed the secret of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, even if he had left it. I fucked her (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5182","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab said: Salem bin Abdullah told me that he heard Abdullah bin Omar speaking that Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, He told us, saying: “When Hafsa bint Omar became a wife to Khunays bin Hudhafa al-Sahmi, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, So he died in Medina, and Omar said: So I went to Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, and presented to him Hafsa bint Omar. He said: I said: If you wish. I married you to Hafsa. He said: I will look into my matter. I stayed for several nights and then he met me and said: It seems to me that I will not get married on this day. He said: Omar: I met Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, and I said to him: If you wish, I will marry you to Hafsa, the daughter of Omar. Abu Bakr remained silent and did not return. I had something to do with him, and I was stronger for him than for Uthman, so I stayed for several nights, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, proposed to her, so I married her. So Abu Bakr told me, and he said: Perhaps you found something wrong with me when you presented Hafsa to me, but I did not return anything to you. Omar said: I said: Yes, he said: Nothing prevented me from returning to you anything about what you presented to me, except that I knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had mentioned it. I would not have revealed the secret of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had left her, I would have kissed her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5183","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam. He said: Abu Bakr, who is Ibn Ayyash, told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah. On the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married her when she was six years old, and he had intercourse with her when she was a girl.” Nine years.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash differed about his name, and it was said: His name is Shu’bah, and it was said: Muhammad, and it was said: His name is his nickname (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5184","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah, meaning Muhammad bin Hazim al-Dair, told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married her when she was six years old, and he had children with her when she was nine years old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5185","Muhammad ibn al-Nadr ibn Musawar al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Ja`far ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me for seven years, and he lived with me for nine years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5186","Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Kufi told us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “He married her.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when she was nine years old, and he died on her behalf when she was eighteen years old.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5187","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abthar told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, who is Ibn Tarif al-Kufi, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, he said: Aisha said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married me for nine years, and I was with him for nine.” Israel disagreed with him in its chain of transmission and text."
"5188","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Adam, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, On the authority of his father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Aisha when she was six years old, and he had children with her when she was nine years old.” He told us Abu Abd al-Rahman: Mutarrif bin Tarif al-Kufi is more steadfast than Israel, and his hadith is more likely to be authentic, and God knows best."
"5189","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The unmarried woman has more right to herself than her guardian, and the virgin asks for permission for herself, and her permission is her fasts.” \""
5190"""
"5190","Mahmud ibn Ghaylan informed us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, who said: I heard from him a year after the death of Nafi', and he had a study circle at that time. He said: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Fadl informed me, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A previously married woman (ayyim) has more right to herself than her guardian, and a virgin is consulted, and her permission is her silence."""
"5191","Ahmed bin Saeed Al-Rabati told me, he said: Ya’qub told us, and he is the son of Abraham, he said: my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: he told me Saleh bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl bin Al-Abbas bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slave woman has more right to her affairs, and the orphan woman is to be appointed in her own right, and by her permission \Her deafness\"""""
"5192","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The master has no authority over the married woman, and the orphan woman is to be consulted, so I kept her silent.”"
"5193","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A married woman has more right to her own life, and a virgin is to be controlled by her father, and with her permission \Her deafness\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5194","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaika, talking about Dhakwan, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Take care of the women regarding their private parts.” It was said: “The virgin is shy.” And she remained silent. He said: This is her permission. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5195","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana'ani told me, he said: Khalid, who is Ibn al-Harith, told us, he said: Hisham, who is al-Dastawi, told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him And he greeted him. He said: “Do not marry a slave woman until she is consulted, and do not marry a virgin until she is consulted.” They said: O Messenger of God, and how is her permission? He said: That \Shut up\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5196","Yahya ibn Durust al-Basri informed us, saying: Abu Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Yahya narrated to us, that Abu Salamah narrated to him, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A previously married woman shall not be married until her permission is sought, and a virgin shall not be married until she is consulted."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah, how is her permission?"" He said: ""Her permission is that she remains silent."""
"5197","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, meaning Ibn Saeed, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, he said: He told me Abu Salamah said, “A man married his daughter in marriage while she was unwilling, so she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Indeed,” and he mentioned a word. It means: My father married me to a man, and I was unwilling, and a cousin of mine proposed to me, and he said: There is no marriage for him, marry whomever you want.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5198","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, and Muhammad told us Bin Salamah, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd The Most Gracious, and the two sons of Yazid bin Jariyah Al-Ansari gathered, on the authority of Khansaa bint Khudham: “Her father married her off while she was married, but she disliked that, so she went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God grant him peace, and he returned his marriage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5199","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr told us, he said: Abu Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The orphan woman is to be appointed by herself, and if she remains silent then it is her permission, and if she refuses then it is not permissible for her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5200","Muhammad ibn Hatim ibn Nu`aym ibn Abd al-Karim al-Marwazi informed us. He said: I am Habban, meaning Ibn Musa. He said: I am Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak. On the authority of Sufyan, meaning Ibn Sa`id, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of Khansaa bint Khudham, she said: “ My father married me when I was unwilling, and I was a virgin. So I complained about that to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Do not marry her when she is unwilling. “Malik ibn Anas disagreed with him in his chain of transmission and in his wording.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5201","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of Ubayy, on the authority of Abd The Most Gracious, and the two sons of Yazid bin Jariyah Al-Ansari, on the authority of Khansaa bint Khudham: “Her father married her off while she was married, so she disliked that, so she went to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God grant him peace, and he returned his marriage.”"
"5202","Muawiyah bin Salih told me, he said: Al-Hakam bin Musa told us, he said: Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir that A man married off his daughter while she was a virgin without her command, so she came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he separated them. “Ahmad ibn Abd told us. Al-Wahid Al-Dimashqi, he said: Abu Hafs told us, meaning Amr bin Abi Salamah Al-Tanisi, he said: I heard Al-Awza’i, he said: Ibrahim bin Murrah told me, On the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, he said: A man married off his daughter while she was a virgin. He narrated the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5203","Ahmad bin Uthman bin Hakim Al-Kufi told us, he said: Ja’far bin Aoun told us, he said: Rabi’ah bin Uthman told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya. Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Nahar al-Abdi, who was an exemplary civilian, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, who said: A man brought his daughter to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and he said: This is my daughter. She refused to get married. He said: Obey your father. All of that. She repeated her statement to him, and she said: “By the One who sent you Truly, I will not get married until you tell me what the husband’s rights are over his wife. He said: The husband’s rights over his wife: If he has an ulcer and she licks it, She did not fulfill his right, and she said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry. So he said: Do not marry them except with their permission. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Harun Al-Abdi, the hadith is abandoned, and his name is Amara bin Juwayn, and Abu Harun Al-Ghanawi, there is nothing wrong with him, and his name is Ibrahim bin Al-Ala. They are both from Basra (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5204","Muhammad bin Dawud al-Masisi told us, he said: Husayn bin Muhammad told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: “A virgin girl came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: My father married me in marriage while she was unwilling.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, responded. Fuck her (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5205","Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Raqqi told me. He said: Muammar, who is the son of Sulaiman al-Raqi, told us. He said: Zayd ibn Hibban told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, said: “A man from Banu al-Mundhir married his unwilling daughter, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he responded.” Her marriage.” Ayoub bin Muhammad told me, he said: Muammar told us, he said: Zayd told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet May God bless him and grant him peace, likewise (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5206","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told me, he said: Ali bin Ghurab told us, he said: Khams bin Al-Hassan told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, on the authority of Aisha said that a girl came in and said: “My father married his brother’s son in marriage to me to remove his meanness through me, and I am unwilling.” She said: Sit until The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, comes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came, and I informed him. He sent for her father and summoned him, and he made the matter To her, she said: O Messenger of God, I have accepted what my father did, but I wanted to teach the women something about the matter.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This hadith they transmit (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5207","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Salih ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The master has no authority with the married woman, and the orphan woman is allowed to be kept alive, so her silence is her consent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5208","Ahmad ibn Sa`id al-Marwazi al-Rabbati told us, he said: Ya’qub is the son of Abraham, he said: my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: he told me Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Jubayr bin Mut’im, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “The mother-in-law has more right to her affairs, and the orphan woman is to be appointed in her own affairs, and her ear is her deafness.”"
"5209","Othman bin Abdullah bin Kharzaz of Antioch told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ataa, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married Maimuna while it was forbidden. She left her matter to Abbas, so he married her.” “Him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is a good chain of narration, and his saying: She made her affairs up to al-Abbas and he married her to him is objectionable. It is as if this letter was from someone who narrated this hadith and was included in the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5210","Muhammad bin Maadan bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he is the son of Muawiyah, he said: Yahya told us, he is the son of Saeed Al-Ansari, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Any woman who is married without the command of her master, her marriage is invalid, and the one who gave her only what he made lawful from her. If they quarrel, that is up to the Sultan, and the Sultan is the guardian of those who have no guardian.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5211","Ahmad bin Sinan al-Wasiti told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, and Ismail bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Anas, that Abu Talha “proposed to Sulaym’s mother, and she said: O Abu Talha, is not your God whom you worship a piece of wood that grew out of the earth?” An Ethiopian, the son of so-and-so, dug it out. He said: Yes. She said: Do not accompany me if you worship a tree that grows in the earth. It was dug up by an Ethiopian, the son of so-and-so. You have converted to Islam. I do not want anything from you other than that. He said: Until I look into my matter. He said: So he went away and then came back and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. And that Muhammad is the Messenger of God. She said: O Anas, marry Abu Talha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5212","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim bin Aliya told us, saying: Yazid told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit al-Bunani, he said: Ibn Umar ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Umm Salamah, “When her waiting period had ended, Abu Bakr sent to her to propose to her, but he did not He married him, then he sent Omar to her to propose to her, but she did not marry him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent to her Omar bin Al-Khattab. He proposed to her, and she said: Tell the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that I am someone else’s wife, and that I am a young woman, and no one My friends are witnesses, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and mentioned that to him, and he said: Go back to her, and say to her: As for what you said? I am a jealous woman: I will pray to God for you and he will take away your jealousy. As for your saying that I am a young woman: your children will be enough for you. Your saying that none of my guardians is a witness: none of your guardians is a witness, nor is anyone absent who hates that, so she said to her son: O Omar, “Arise and marry the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he married him.” Summary (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5213","Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sabiq told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Any woman to whom a guardian is given in marriage, it belongs to the first of them, and whoever If a man sells something to two men, it belongs to the first.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5214","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samura, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a guardian is married, then he is the first.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5215","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Sulayman bin al-Mughirah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, he said: “When Zainab’s waiting period had passed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Zaid: ‘Remember her to me.’ Zaid said: So I set off, so I said O Zainab, give me good news. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to remind you. She said: I will not do anything until I seek the advice of my Lord. So she got up to her mosque, and the Qur’an was revealed, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came until he entered upon her without an order.”"
"5216","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: I am Al-Mulai, and his name is Al-Fadl bin Dakin, Abu Nu’aym, he said: Issa told us, and he is Ibn Tahman Abu Bakr, he said: I heard Anas, saying: “Zainab used to boast about the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying that God had given me marriage from heaven, and in her The verse about the veil was revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5217","Ahmad bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Nu`aym told us, he said: Issa told us, meaning Ibn Tahman Abu Bakr, I heard Anas bin Malik, He says: Zainab bint Jahsh used to boast about the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God Almighty granted me marriage from heaven, and in it The verse about the veil was revealed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5218","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad, who is Ibn Zayd, told us, on the authority of Matar Al-Warraq, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Abi Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “He married Maimuna while it was lawful, and he married her while it was lawful. And I was the messenger between them.” Malik ibn Anas sent him"
"5219","Amr bin Hisham Al-Harrani informed us, saying: Mukhlid told us, meaning Ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ja`far, meaning Ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maymun, meaning Ibn Mihran. On the authority of Safiyya, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimuna while it was lawful, and he built extravagance with her, and it was Maimuna’s grave.” extravagantly"
"5220","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Tahman, told me about Al-Hajjaj, who is Ibn Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid, who is Ibn Zuran, on the authority of Maymoon bin Mihran, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of his paternal aunt. Maimuna, because she told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married her lawfully, and he built lawful relations with her, and he married her extravagantly. And he built it under depletion.”"
"5221","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad, meaning treachery, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, he said: “He did not marry The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, met Maimunah while he was in ihram, and she was Yazid’s aunt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5222","Ahmad bin Nasr al-Naysaburi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Musa, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married Maimuna while he was in ihram.”"
"5223","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, meaning Ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha, that Ibn Abbas, He told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “married Maimuna while he was in a state of ihram.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5224","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, who said: Abu Awanah, whose name is Waddah, narrated to us, on the authority of al-Mughirah, on the authority of Shebak. On the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married some of his wives while he was in ihram.”"
"5225","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abu Asim, who is Al-Nabil, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Aisha, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He got married while in ihram.” I said to Abu Asim: You dictated to us this matter of companionship that does not include Aisha. He said: Leave Aisha so I can look into it."
"5226","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sawa, he said: Saeed, meaning Ibn Abi Arouba, told us on the authority of Qatada, and Ali bin Hakim, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maimuna bint Al-Harith while he was in a state of ihram,” and in a hadith Ya’la: “extravagantly.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5227","Othman bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told me, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “married Maimuna while he was in a state of ihram. She turned her matter over to Abbas, so he married her to him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5228","Ahmad bin Nasr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah, who is Ibn Musa, told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He married Maimuna while he was in ihram.”"
"5229","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Maan told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Nabih bin Wahb, that Aban bin Othman, he said: I heard Othman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A person in ihram shall not marry, nor shall \And he does not get engaged.\"""""
"5230","Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad ibn Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli Al-Basri narrated to us, saying: Yazid narrated to us, meaning Ibn Zurai’, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, meaning Ibn Abu Orouba, on the authority of Mutarrif, and Ya`la ibn Hakim, on the authority of Nabih ibn Wahb, on the authority of Aban ibn Uthman, that Uthman ibn Affan, may God be pleased with him It was narrated on the authority of him, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “A person in ihram shall not marry, nor shall he be married, nor shall he be engaged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5231","Wahb bin Bayan told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Urwa bin Al-Zubayr told him On the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, “Umm Habiba, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God,” I marry my father’s daughter, meaning: Her sister. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do you like that? She said: Yes, I am not close to you, and I love the one who shares my goodness with my sister. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is not permissible. Umm Habibah said: O Messenger of God, by God, we have spoken that you would marry Durrat bint Abi Salamah. He said: Umm Salamah’s daughter? Umm Habiba said: Yes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: By God, if she had not been my stepdaughter under my guardianship, she would not have been lawful for me. She is my foster-brother’s daughter, so do not introduce your daughters or your sisters to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5232","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, that Zainab, the daughter of Umm Salamah, She told him, “Umm Habibah said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ‘We have told you that you are married to Durra bint Abi Salamah. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Is she superior to Umm Salama? “If I had not married Umm Salamah, she would not have been lawful for me, for her father is my breastfeeding brother.”"
"5233","Imran bin Bakkar Al-Barrad Al-Humsi told us, he said: Abu Al-Yaman told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, he said: Urwa told me that Zainab was the daughter of Abu Salamah, and her mother was Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She told him that Umm Habibah was the daughter of Abu Sufyan, she informed her that she said: O Messenger of God, “Marry my sister, the daughter of Abu Sufyan.” She said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: Or do you like that? She said: Yes, I am not estranged, and I love whoever shares my goodness with my sister. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: This is not permissible for me, so I said: By God, O Messenger of God, we are talking about you wanting to marry Durrat bint Abi Salamah. He said: Umm Salamah’s daughter? I said: Yes. He said: By God, had she not been my stepdaughter and under my guardianship, she would not have been lawful for me. She is the daughter of my foster brother. She breastfed me. And her father is Thuwaiba, so do not present your daughters or your sisters to me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5234","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abda, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of Umm Habiba, she said: O Messenger of God, “Do you have anything to do with my sister?” He said: What should I do? She said: Marry her. He said: For that is what I love. To you? She said: Yes, I am not close to you, and I love the one who associates with me in the good of my sister. He said: She is not permissible for me. She said: For he has informed me. Are you proposing to Durrat, the daughter of Umm Salamah? He said: The daughter of Umm Salamah. She said: Yes. He said: By God, if she were not my stepdaughter, she would not be permissible for me. She is To my foster-brother’s daughter. He said: “Do not present your daughters or your sisters to me.”"
"5235","Mujahid bin Musa told us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He forbade The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, required that a woman be married to her paternal aunt, or to her paternal maternal aunt.”"
"5236","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Ma’an, who is Ibn Isa, told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj On the authority of Abu Hurairah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman and her paternal aunt should not be brought together, nor should a woman be married to her maternal aunt.”"
"5237","Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Abdul Wahhab bin Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam informed us, he said: Muhammad told us Ibn Fulayh, on the authority of Yunus, Ibn Shihab said: Qubaysah ibn Dhu’ayb told me that he heard Abu Hurairah say: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, that a woman and her paternal aunt should be brought together, and a woman and her maternal aunt should be brought together.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5238","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Yahya bin Ayyub told us, that Ja’far bin Rabi’ah told him, On the authority of Arak bin Malik, and Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that: “He forbade being married “The woman is on her paternal aunt or paternal aunt.”"
"5239","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He forbade four women from being brought together: the woman and her paternal aunt, and the woman and her paternal aunt.”"
"5240","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, that Abu Salamah told him, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “A woman should not be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her paternal maternal aunt.”"
"5241","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Muhammad told us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “A woman should not be married to her paternal aunt, or to her paternal aunt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5242","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, he said: Ayoub bin Musa told me, on the authority of Bukayr Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And peace be upon him, he said: “A woman may not be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her paternal aunt.”"
"5243","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi told us, on the authority of Abda, he is the son of Suleiman, and Muhammad means Ibn Ubaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yaqoub Bin Utba, on the authority of Sulayman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He forbids putting things together.” Muhammad said: For a man to bring a woman and her paternal aunt together, and a woman and her paternal aunt. Bukair Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5244","Amr bin Mansour Al-Nasa’i told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Layth, who is Ibn Saad, told us, he said: Ayoub bin Musa told me, On the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A woman shall not be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her paternal maternal aunt.”"
"5245","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim al-Kufi informed us, saying: Bakr told us, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Rabah al-Makki, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “A woman shall not be married On her paternal aunt, and not on her paternal aunt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5246","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir told us that he is Ibn Sulaiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, On the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a woman to marry her paternal aunt, and a paternal aunt to a daughter.” Her brother “Ibn Aoun made him stop.”"
"5247","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-Sana'ani told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn al-Harith, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “A woman should not be married off to her paternal aunt or her paternal aunt.” He said: “And a woman should not be married off to her brother’s daughter or her sister’s daughter.” Asim disagreed with them. Bin Suleiman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5248","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of al-Shabi, he said: I heard Jabir, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “peace and blessings of God be upon him, that a woman may be married to her paternal aunt and paternal aunt.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5249","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Asim told me, he said: I read a letter to Al-Sha’bi. In it, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “A woman should not be married to her paternal aunt, nor to her paternal maternal aunt.” I heard this from Jabir. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5250","5253 Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “The Messenger of God forbade May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a woman may be married to her paternal aunt or paternal aunt.”"
"5251","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “He is forbidden by breastfeeding what is forbidden by lineage.” Hisham bin Urwa disagreed with him and said: On the authority of Abd Allah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5252","Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Kufi told us, he said: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, and Musa bin Abdul Rahman told me, He said: Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, she said: I heard Aisha, It says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What is forbidden from breastfeeding is what is forbidden from childbirth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5253","5291 Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, meaning Al-Qattan, he said: Malik told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dinar told me On the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whatever childbirth made forbidden, breastfeeding made forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5254","Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Al-Mughirah Al-Homsi told us, saying: Othman, meaning Ibn Sa’id bin Kathir bin Dinar Al-Homsi, told us, on the authority of Shuaib, meaning Ibn Abi Hamza Al-Homsi said: I asked Al-Zuhri: What is forbidden from breastfeeding? He said: Urwa told me that Aisha used to say: Deprive of breastfeeding whom you deprive of lineage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5255","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Baghdadi Al-Makhrami informed us, saying: Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa’id. Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ali, I said: O Messenger of God, “Shall I not direct you to the most beautiful girl in Quraysh?” He said: Who is she? I said: The daughter of Hamza. He said: Did you not know that she is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding, and that God has forbidden through breastfeeding what he has forbidden through lineage? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5256","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdullah bin Bakr told us, he said: Saeed is the son of Abi Arouba, on the authority of Ali bin Zaid, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “that Ali said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace,” about the daughter of Hamza, and he mentioned who Her beauty, so he said: She is the daughter of my brother through breastfeeding. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Did you not know that God has forbidden her through breastfeeding? What is forbidden from lineage? \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"5257","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Saeed bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Ali said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “about the daughter of Hamza,” and he mentioned her beauty, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: She is my brother’s daughter through breastfeeding. Did you not know that God has forbidden through breastfeeding what He has forbidden through lineage?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5258","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whatever was forbidden through lineage is forbidden through breastfeeding.” Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim told me, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly"
"5259","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad told us, meaning treacherous, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “He is forbidden from breastfeeding what is forbidden from childbirth.” Then he said, “After lineage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5260","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She told him “that her paternal uncle by breastfeeding, whose name is Aflah, asked her for permission, but she blocked him, so she told the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He greeted him and said: “Do not cover yourself with him, for he is deprived of breastfeeding what is forbidden by lineage.”"
"5261","Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Taymi Al-Qadi told me, saying: Yahya bin Saeed, who is Al-Qattan, told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The daughter of Hamza was mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: She is the daughter of my brother from Breastfeeding.” Shu’bah said: This was heard by Qatada from Jabir ibn Zayd. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5262","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Sulami, on the authority of Ali Radi God on his authority. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, “Why are you fighting among the Quraysh and leaving us?” He said: And do you have anyone with you? I said: Yes, daughter of Hamza. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: She is not permissible for me, she is my breastfeeding brother’s daughter."
"5263","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sawa told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “went to the daughter of Hamza, and he said: She is my brother’s daughter through breastfeeding.” And he is deprived of breastfeeding what is forbidden by lineage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5264","Harun bin Abdullah al-Hammal told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “There were ten breastfeedings in what was revealed of the Qur’an.” \""
5265"""
"5265","Al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman ibn Dawud informed us, saying: Abu al-Aswad, whose name is al-Nadr ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar, and Ishaq ibn Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, saying: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'ah, that Ibn Shihab wrote mentioning that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed him, from 'A'ishah, who said: Abu Hudhayfah ibn 'Utbah ibn Rabi'ah had adopted Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah — and it is said: a woman of the Ansar had freed him — until the verse was revealed concerning them: ""Call them by [the names of] their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah"" (33:5). So Sahlah bint Suhayl, the wife of Abu Hudhayfah, came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, we adopted Salim, and Allah has revealed concerning him what you know; he enters upon me, and I am a grown woman, and we have only one house."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Suckle him."" So she suckled him five times, and he would enter upon her, and Salim was at that time a grown man."
"5266","Yahya bin Hakim Al-Basri informed us, saying: Ibn Abi Adiy told us, and Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sucking and the two suckings are not forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5267","Ziyad bin Ayyub Dalawayh told me, he said: Ibn Ulayyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, meaning Ibn Kaysan al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulaika, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sucking and the two suckings are not forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5268","Yazid bin Sinan Al-Basri told me, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Al-Khalil, whose name is Salih, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his paternal aunt Aisha, that she said: “He is only forbidden from breastfeeding seven times,” he said. Abu Abd al-Rahman: It was narrated by Khaled, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih Abi al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin al-Harith, on the authority of Musika On the authority of Aisha, and Yazid bin Zuray’ said, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha"
"5269","Abdullah bin Al-Sabbah bin Abdullah Al-Attar Al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Sawa told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada And Ayoub, on the authority of Salih Abi Al-Khalil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal, on the authority of Umm Al-Fadl, that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said: He was asked about breastfeeding, and he said: It is not forbidden to have one stroke or two strokes, and Qatada said: sucking and two suckings. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5270","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith. On the authority of Umm Al-Fadl, that a man from Banu Amir bin Sa’sa’ah said: O Messenger of God, “Is a single breastfeeding forbidden?” He said: “No.” He said: Abu Abd al-Rahman: It was narrated by Urwa, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not mention Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5271","Shuaib bin Yusuf Al-Nasa’i told me, on the authority of Yahya Al-Qattan, on the authority of Hisham, who is Ibn Urwa. He said: My father told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The sucking and the two suckings are not forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5272","Ubayd Allah bin Fadalah bin Ibrahim Al-Nasa’i told me, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muhammad bin Dinar told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “The sucking and the two suckings are not forbidden. And the imlaja, and the two imlaja” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5273","Ahmad ibn Harb al-Mawsili informed us, he said: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, and Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: “Do not deprive “Al-Massah” and “Al-Massatan”"
"5274","Abdul-Warith bin Abdul-Samad bin Abdul-Warith told us, he said: My father told me, he said: My father told me, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I am alcoholic. On the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “There is nothing wrong with sucking or sucking, but rather breastfeeding is what splits the intestines.” Muhammad ibn Ishaq disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5275","Muhammad bin Mansour al-Tusi told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, who is the son of Ibrahim bin Saad, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: He told me Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Aslami, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Neither sucking nor sucking is forbidden from breastfeeding. Rather, what is expressed from the milk is forbidden from breastfeeding.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5276","Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Musaysi told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Uqba, he said: Urwa used to narrate, On the authority of Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “One and two suckings are not forbidden from breastfeeding, nor are “It is forbidden from it, except for milk that ruptures the intestines.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5277","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid bin Zuray’ told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: We wrote to We asked Ibrahim bin Yazid al-Nakha’i about breastfeeding, and he wrote that Shurayh told us that Ali and Ibn Masoud used to say: He is deprived of Breastfeeding, little or much, and it was in his book that Abu Al-Sha’a’ Al-Muharbibi told us that Aisha told him that the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He used to say: “A kidnapping or two kidnappings is not forbidden.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"5278","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’atha’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, he said: She said: Aisha: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me while there was a man sitting with me. This became intense for him, and I saw anger on his face, so I said: O Messenger of God, “He is my brother through breastfeeding.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Look at your brothers.” And he said again: “Look who Your brothers from breastfeeding, for breastfeeding is from famine.”"
"5279","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not forbidden from breastfeeding except that which has herniated the intestines in the breast, and that was before weaning.”"
"5280","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Abdullah, meaning Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: “No one is forbidden from breastfeeding except that which has herniated the intestines.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
